Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the CityLink Project

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version 2.0.1)
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Integration in App.jsx
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the main App div, after the Footer component
- Placement ensures analytics tracking is active across all routes while maintaining proper component hierarchy

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart):
- For React/Vite projects, the `@vercel/analytics/react` import is used
- The Analytics component was added to the root App component to track all page views and interactions
- The component is self-contained and doesn't require additional configuration

## Project Framework
- Framework: React + Vite
- Package Manager: npm
- Project Type: Single Page Application with React Router

## Verification Steps Completed
1. ✅ Successfully installed @vercel/analytics package
2. ✅ Added Analytics component to App.jsx following React/Vite best practices
3. ✅ Build completed successfully (vite build)
4. ✅ No new linting errors introduced (existing errors were pre-existing)

## Next Steps for Deployment
After deploying to Vercel:
1. Navigate to the Vercel project dashboard
2. Select "Analytics" from the sidebar
3. Click "Enable" to activate analytics tracking
4. Analytics data will start appearing after deployment and user visits
5. Verify by checking browser Network tab for analytics requests to `/_vercel/insights/*`

## Files Modified
- `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and dependencies
- `frontend/src/App.jsx` - Added Analytics import and component

## Notes
- The Analytics component is lightweight and doesn't impact application performance
- It automatically tracks page views and web vitals
- No additional configuration is required for basic analytics
- All data is collected in compliance with privacy regulations
